---
// Shared "config file handling" note for package-based (.deb / .rpm) upgrades.
// Single source of truth for this guidance, rendered by LinuxUpgradeSteps,
// TrendzUpgradeSteps, and the CE-to-PE upgrade page. There is no "merge" option
// in the package managers; the recommended flow is to base off the new file and
// carry custom values over.
import { Aside } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

interface Props {
	platform: 'ubuntu' | 'centos';
}

const { platform } = Astro.props;
const isUbuntu = platform === 'ubuntu';
---

<Aside type="caution" title="Configuration files">
	{isUbuntu ? (
		<>
			<p><code>dpkg</code> asks how to handle a configuration file (<code>[Y/I/N/O/D/Z]</code>) only if you modified that file and the new package contains a different version.</p>
			<p>If no prompt appears, your existing configuration is preserved and no additional action is required.</p>
			<p>If prompted, use the new package configuration as the base:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Press <strong>Y</strong> to install the package maintainer's version.</li>
				<li>Your previous configuration is saved with the <code>.dpkg-old</code> suffix.</li>
				<li>Copy your custom settings from the <code>.dpkg-old</code> file into the new configuration.</li>
			</ol>
			<p><strong>Important:</strong> complete the configuration update before running the database upgrade. The upgrade script uses this configuration to connect to the database.</p>
		</>
	) : (
		<>
			<p>If your existing configuration was modified and the package contains an updated version, <code>rpm</code> preserves your current configuration and may create the new package configuration with the <code>.rpmnew</code> suffix. If no <code>.rpmnew</code> file appears, no additional action is required.</p>
			<p>Compare the configuration files and transfer your custom settings before continuing.</p>
			<p><strong>Important:</strong> make sure the resulting configuration contains the correct database connection and all required custom settings before running the database upgrade.</p>
		</>
	)}
</Aside>
